```

Current bug report: {'summary': 'LookupTranslator accepts CharSequence as input, but fails to work with implementations other than String', 'description': 'The core of org.apache.commons.lang3.text.translate is a HashMap<CharSequence, CharSequence> lookupMap.\nFrom the Javadoc of CharSequence (emphasis mine):\n> \n> This interface does not refine the general contracts of the equals and hashCode methods. The result of comparing two objects that implement CharSequence is therefore, in general, undefined. Each object may be implemented by a different class'}

